<title>FRANCE: NYK top gateway for ADP Jan-Sept imports.</title>
<headline>NYK top gateway for ADP Jan-Sept imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top airport gateway for imports to Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>January-September 1996 New York-Paris air cargo volume totalled 29,461 tonnes, down five percent on the same period last year, ADP figures showed.</p>
<p>In second place, was Chicago, with 21,838 tonnes, an increase of 14.8 percent on the first nine months of 1995.</p>
<p>Hong Kong was ranked third with 14,338 tonnes flown ex-Paris last month, a fall of 6.3 percent on 1995 levels, ADP said.</p>
<p>The top ten airport gateways for ADP imports between January and September 1996 and the percentage change on the same period in 1995 were as follows:</p>
<p>    City		 Tonnes	     Pct change from</p>
<p>						  a year ago</p>
<p> 1  New York	   29,461 tonnes    -5.0pct</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	    21,838 tonnes    +14.8</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong	  14,338 tonnes     -6.3</p>
<p> 4  Los Angeles	12,603 tonnes     -6.4</p>
<p> 5  Tokyo		11,749 tonnes    -17.0</p>
<p> 6  Montreal	   10,088 tonnes     +0.3</p>
<p> 7. Miami		 5,576 tonnes     -4.0</p>
<p> 8  Casablanca	  4,588 tonnes    -10.4</p>
<p> 9  Dubai		 4,122 tonnes     +0.6</p>
<p> 10 Johannesburg	3,915 tonnes    +21.9</p>
